version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-10
abstract: >
  Field notes for driving an unmodified computer from an automation agent,
  using a Linux machine in the Bluetooth HID device role to deliver keystrokes
  and pointer motion, and a USB video capture device to read the target's
  screen back as frames. The target needs no driver, agent, service or account,
  so the same method reaches a locked desktop, a firmware menu, a console or a
  phone. The documentation covers the system-level changes a bridge host needs,
  the HID report descriptor and wire format for a combined keyboard and mouse,
  how many radios a given number of clients requires, the manual pairing step
  that cannot be automated, and the failure modes of each. Code is illustrative
  rather than a product, on the expectation that readers scaffold an
  implementation for their own environment with a coding agent.
